{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sharing-state-between-components","statement":"Almaty was the capital city of Kazakhstan from 1929 to 1997.","source_span":"From 1929 to 1997, it was its capital city."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sharing-state-between-components","statement":"The name Almaty comes from the Kazakh word 'алма', meaning 'apple', often translated as 'full of apples'.","source_span":"The name comes from <span lang=\"kk-KZ\">алма</span>, the Kazakh word for \"apple\" and is often translated as \"full of apples\"."}
